<title>ITALY: Italy govt calls confidence vote on bank.</title>
<headline>Italy govt calls confidence vote on bank.</headline>
<dateline>ROME 1996-11-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Italian government has called a confidence vote in the Senate (upper house) to convert into law a decree on a rescue plan for the country's biggest southern bank, Banco di Napoli, and two other decrees.</p>
<p>The decision, announced in the Senate by Regional Affairs Minister Franco Bassanini, to sweep away opposition amendments blocking passage. The confidence call was also made for two other decrees though it was not immediately clear whether three separate votes would be held.</p>
</text>
